# Another gem's require makes a gem `convention-only` (DEC-670), but only a
# require that loads the gem: runner_kit's `require_relative "parallel_x"`
# loads its own file; loose, which requires json_x, is itself a row, so it
# only lowers json_x: nothing is seen to load loose, though a Railtie may
# (better_errors loading binding_of_caller). framer, which the app uses, requiring
# addon without depending on it is the case the rule is for.
dead Gemfile parallel_x=unreferenced~ json_x=unreferenced~row addon=convention-only~ loose=unreferenced~ runner_kit=none framer=none
